# Beads kept local-only: issues live in the Dolt DB, not git.
# Auto-exported JSONL churns on every bd mutation, so it's not tracked.
# (git hooks disabled via: git config --unset core.hooksPath)
# .beads/issues.jsonl is deliberately TRACKED. It is bd's passive export, not
# the issue store — Dolt is — and not a full backup: `bd import` rebuilds the
# issues from it, but Dolt's own history does not survive the round trip. It
# is the recovery floor, and worth having because while this line ignored it,
# bd's auto-export failed silently on every write (its `git add` was refused)
# and beads existed nowhere but one laptop — until a stray rm -rf on
# 2026-07-27 took it out.
.beads/interactions.jsonl

# Private strategy notes — the honest version of the uptake stall; not for the public repo.
